z$ ($x = 0$, $y = 0$) of the same wave. The metric on it is $f(-c^2dt^2 + dz^2)$, and the factor drops out of the null condition, so for every $f$ the rays are at 45°, and they are null geodesics.","The two pulses leave the singularity $t = 0$ as one, about $z = 0$, and run apart along the marked rays $z = \\pm ct$. Far ahead of them and far behind them $x$ and $y$ expand alike, as in the Kasner universe the wave was built on."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains","einstein_tensor"],"version":"36560c128eea184e"},"slices":[{"view":"tube","surface":0,"curve":0,"label":"$\\tau = 0.25$","version":"a843b59ff7e8d53f","lines":[],"points":[[0.5,0.0421]],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.5,0.0421],"anchor":"bl","dx":5.1,"dy":-5.1}},{"view":"tube","surface":0,"curve":1,"label":"$\\tau = 0.5$","version":"706c38d6cdb4a50f","lines":[],"points":[[0.5,0.0868]],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.5,0.0868],"anchor":"br","dx":-5.1,"dy":-5.1}},{"view":"tube","surface":0,"curve":2,"label":"$\\tau = 1$","version":"2359b49911ffdaed","lines":[],"points":[[0.5,0.1959]],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.5,0.1959],"anchor":"bl","dx":5.1,"dy":-5.1}},{"view":"tube","surface":0,"curve":3,"label":"$\\tau = 2$","version":"55d97762fb413c1c","lines":[],"points":[[0.5,0.6045]],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.5,0.6045],"anchor":"bl","dx":5.1,"dy":-5.1}},{"view":"ring","surface":0,"label":"$\\tau = 0.25$","version":"bfc99f0d520cd248","lines":[],"points":[[0.5,0.0421]],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.5,0.0421],"anchor":"bl","dx":5.1,"dy":-5.1}},{"view":"ring","surface":1,"label":"$\\tau = 0.5$","version":"8c970f73b13cb810","lines":[],"points":[[0.5,0.0868]],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.5,0.0868],"anchor":"bl","dx":5.1,"dy":-5.1}},{"view":"ring","surface":2,"label":"$\\tau = 1$","version":"ccdc55c8405ff0e0","lines":[],"points":[[0.5,0.1959]],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.5,0.1959],"anchor":"bl","dx":5.1,"dy":-5.1}},{"view":"ring","surface":3,"label":"$\\ta